# Shell scripts must check out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true by default) converts the
# committed LF blob to CRLF in the working tree. A CRLF shell script can fail
# under stricter shells: the shebang is read as "bash\r" and every line carries
# a trailing carriage return that corrupts variable values and comparisons.
# Claude Code installs this plugin by cloning the repo, so a Windows installer
# would get the converted copy.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else interpreted by a POSIX shell.
*.bash text eol=lf
